  "id": "COMPOUND:30048 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Isodaucene appears to have a complex target relationship with U373 MG, mediated through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Isodaucene targets Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside and (2Alpha,3Beta,17R*,18Beta)-23-O-(Cis-P-Coumaroyl)-19(18->17)-Abeo-28-Norolean-12-Ene-2,3,18-Triol. All these compounds ultimately target U373 MG, indicating a potential hierarchical pathway where Isodaucene may act through a common intermediate, Thioredoxin, to influence U373 MG. The overlapping targets and the consistent final destination of U373 MG suggest a possible functional link between Isodaucene and U373 MG, possibly through a shared mechanism involving mitochondrial thioredoxin. The evidence supports a mechanism where Isodaucene may modulate the activity of Thioredoxin, which in turn affects U373 MG, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
